  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Of the following four aqueous solutions, the total number of those solutions whose freezing point is lower than that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>MC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></math> is (Integer answer)<br />(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Ba</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br />(ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math><br />(iii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>KCl</mi></math><br />(iv) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ik</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> is&nbsp;the same for all solutions so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> depends on Van&#39;t Hoff factor (i). Greater is i small is freezing point.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\" columnlines=\"solid\" frame=\"solid\" rowlines=\"solid\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>&#160;Compound&#160;</mtext></mtd><mtd><mtext>&#160;i&#160;</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Ba</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>KCl</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>So the given solutions have a lower freezing point than ethanol.</p>",
